        "number": 335,
        "content": "<div class=\"chapter-header\">\n  <h2 class=\"chapter-title\">Descended into the Tiancang Great Chiliocosm (Part 2)</h2>\n  <span class=\"chapter-number\">Chapter 335</span>\n</div>\n<hr class=\"chapter-divider\">\n10,000 Years In A Cultivation Sect: I Ob... \nChapter 335: Descended into the Tiancang Great Chiliocosm (Part 2)\n\nJiang Ming was looking at some secrets and prying into something weird. When he flipped to a page, he frowned.\n\nIt was a page about Ye Qingxian.\n\n‘She’s actually returned to reality!’\n\nShe had stayed in the Supreme Pagoda for almost a year, which was akin to about a thousand years inside.\n\nJiang Ming didn’t expect her to return to reality.\n!!\n\nBased on her Status, she seemed to have accumulated to an extreme after she activated the Dao Enlightenment Mode. She had been tempering herself for a long time before she returned to her reality to look around. She planned to continue only after that and tried her best to go through more levels to get herself into the group chat.\n\nHowever, she was in danger.\n\n‘Life-and–death crisis?’ Jiang Ming frowned.\n\nHe knew it was easy for her to escape because of the presence of the Supreme Pagoda. But because of her temperament, he was afraid that…\n\nMoreover, he knew that if the Supreme Pagoda was to be evoked during a battle, it would have a few seconds delay. It was the rule that desperation might be present amidst life.\n\nIn fact, a short while was more than enough to determine one’s life to experts.\n\n‘It’s fate that we met. Since I’ve learned about her condition, I shall try to save her. I’m just wondering if the time flow over there is the same as mine?’ As Jiang Ming thought, he conjured a clone which made its way into the Human Path Record to be projected to that world.\n\nProjection that traversed different worlds was energy consuming. But he managed to endure it this time. He had, after all, become stronger with his improved cultivation base, foundation and energy.\n\nHe briefly calculated that the energy spent this time was less than one third of the energy of the main body, excluding the power of his inner world.\n\n‘I think I can bear it if I go in person!’ As Jiang Ming thought, he closed his eyes to feel the condition of his clone.\n\nWhen the main body and its clone were being separated by great chiliocosm and even the Chaos, even if the telepathy existed between them, it would be greatly reduced.\n\nNevertheless, Jiang Ming had the Human Path Record as the medium.\n\nHe knew that his clone had got to a great chiliocosm of unknown size. There was a force called the Stone Mansion, dominating a territory.\n\nAfter the transcendence of Ye Qingxian, she joined the Stone Mansion and was specifically trained.\n\nJiang Ming’s clone was about 100 miles away from Ye Qingxian. He was concealing himself in the void.\n\nThe moment he got there, Jiang Ming sensed the difference in the world. ‘What’s the difference?’ He frowned, ‘It’s the difference in the origin!’\n\nHe immediately had a judgment. A different origin would cause an imperceptible change in the laws.\n\nA foreigner needed to breathe in the aura here to adapt to the world. He sealed himself with the Human Path Record while absorbing the aura of the world. In no time, his breath had been assimilated.\n\nBesides, with the Records to chop off his karma, no one could calculate his origin.\n\nThen, Jiang Ming began to observe his surroundings. Beneath him was a massive God City. It was 80 thousand miles from east to west, and 30 thousand miles from south to north. It was so massive beyond imagination.\n\nHowever, there was a great war in the city. The city protecting formation was broken. Everywhere in the city was massacre, collision of special abilities, and the flying immortal weapons. There was a continuous rain of blood too.\n\n‘The intruders were merely three Golden Immortals, two of which are only at the initial stage, only one is at the later stage. Hence they aren’t that strong!’ Jiang Ming had already analyzed the situation here, ‘There are only two Golden Immortal defenders. One at his initial stage while another at the middle stage. In short, this was just a common battle.’\n\nIt was known as a common battle because the battle did not involve any brilliant expert or genius. Hence, the situation whereby an expert could fight against someone of a higher cultivation base would not exist.\n\nBesides, it was difficult for an expert to kill another expert of the same cultivation base. Hence, it would take a long time to determine the winner.\n\nSuch a situation was very common in infinite realms.\n\nJiang Ming saw Ye Qingxian. Because he found out that she was safe for now, he didn’t show himself. Instead he invaded the sea of consciousness of some immortals to find out the details of the world here.\n\nThe world where he was, was called the Tiancang Great Chiliocosm. There was a Heaven Court dominating the world even though it was not as strong as the Heaven Court of the Honggu Heavenly Realm.\n\nThe immortal land was divided into 81 provinces. He was currently in Cloud Province, located in the south east direction.\n\nIn Cloud Province were 72 mansions, and this city belonged to the Stone Mansion. The Mansion Master was called Shi Lei, a relatively famous human being.\n\n‘The cause of the battle is rather ridiculous!’ Jiang Ming had a strange feeling when he learned about the cause of the battle.\n\nShi Lei had a younger brother called Shi Han. When he died many years back, he left behind his son, Shi Fang.\n\nShi Fang had many bad habits because of him abusing his social status. But he was clever enough not to provoke people with status in the Stone Mansion. He had been lecherous since young. When he first met Ye Qingxian, he was eager to hit on her. He gave up when he learned that Shi Lei valued Ye Qingxian.\n\nNot long ago, there was a beautiful lady who came to the Stone Mansion. Shi Fang was attracted when he saw her. Before he took action, he secretly inquired about her. He found out that the woman was a foreigner. She had no guardians and she was not strong, only at True Immortal Realm. Hence, he got her into the mansion.\n\nBut he fell for her. Hence, he began pursuing her. He had been sweet talking to her, and even gave her a Mystical Immortal Weapon as a gift. Yet, all his efforts were in vain, and he was scolded instead.\n\nShi Fang had finally lost his patience, and raped her.\n\nThe girl was heartbroken.\n\nHalf a month later when Shi Fang was getting more relaxed, the girl managed to escape. And she was now back to take revenge.\n\nThe girl was called Lan Shuirou, the daughter of the Mansion Master of the Misty Mansion next door. She had been trained in secret all these while.\n\n---\n*End of Chapter 335*\n",
